  "notes": "A compound of {両|りょう} (both) and {目|め} (eye). Straightforward in meaning but useful for distinguishing actions or conditions affecting both eyes versus just one. The prefix {両|りょう} is productive and appears in many similar compounds.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {両目|りょうめ}を{開|あ}ける: to open both eyes\n- {両目|りょうめ}を{閉|と}じる: to close both eyes\n- {両目|りょうめ}で{見|み}る: to look with both eyes\n\nRELATED TERMS WITH {両|りょう}:\n- {両手|りょうて}: both hands\n- {両足|りょうあし}: both legs/feet\n- {両耳|りょうみみ}: both ears\n- {片目|かため}: one eye — the counterpart using {片|かた} (one of a pair)",
